{% comment %}
  Converts legacy HTML post content to markdown — but only when the content
  still looks like legacy Trumbowyg HTML (starts with a tag and contains known
  HTML tags). Already-converted markdown is returned untouched, which keeps
  migration re-runs stable.

  Arguments:
    content - post content string (HTML or markdown), may be nil

  Returns: markdown string (or the original value when no conversion applies)
{% endcomment %}
{% liquid
  assign result = content
  if content != blank
    assign trimmed = content | strip
    assign first_char = trimmed | slice: 0, 1
    assign looks_html = content | matches: '<(p|h[1-6]|ul|ol|li|br|div|span|strong|em|b|i|a|img)[\s>/]'
    if first_char == '<' and looks_html
      function result = 'modules/blog/lib/migrations/html_to_markdown', html: content
    endif
  endif
%}
{% return result %}
